sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor K as Besogende
    participant RM as RegisterModel
    participant RC as IRecaptchaVerifier
    participant US as IUserAccountStore
    participant PL as IPendingLoginStore
    participant ES as IEmailSender
    participant CM as ConfirmLoginModel

    K->>RM: POST /Account/Register (email, name, password, confirm, captcha token)
    Note over RM: [EnableRateLimiting("auth")] - 50 per minute per IP

    alt ModelState invalid
        RM-->>K: Page() with validation errors
        Note over RM: Server rule: StringLength(100, MinimumLength = 8)<br/>and the two passwords must match.<br/>The strength meter on the form is client-side guidance only.
    else valid
        RM->>RC: VerifyAsync(captcha token)
        alt captcha rejected
            RM-->>K: "Bekraeft at du ikke er en robot"
        else captcha ok
            RM->>RM: PasswordHasher.HashPassword (PBKDF2)
            RM->>US: CreateUser(email, hash, name, UserRole.Customer)
            Note over RM,US: Self-registration can only ever create Customer.<br/>Employee and Admin are seeded or created from /Admin/Users.

            alt email already registered
                US-->>RM: false
                RM-->>K: "Der findes allerede en konto med den e-mail"
            else created
                US-->>RM: true
                RM->>US: FindByEmail(email)
                US-->>RM: ApplicationUser
                RM->>PL: Create(userId, safeReturnUrl, 15 min)
                PL-->>RM: raw token (hash stored)
                RM->>US: SetPrefersEnglish(userId), if the site is in English
                RM->>ES: SendAsync("Bekraeft din konto" or "Confirm your account")
                RM-->>K: Redirect to /Account/CheckEmail?purpose=register
            end
        end
    end

    K->>CM: GET /Account/ConfirmLogin?token=...
    CM->>PL: Consume(token)
    CM->>US: RecordActivity(userId)
    CM->>CM: SignInAsync (auth cookie with the security stamp)
    CM->>CM: merge the guest cart, and move a guest order just placed<br/>in this session into the new account, if the email matches
    CM-->>K: signed in, redirected

    Note over K,CM: Registration does not sign you in.<br/>The same proof-of-inbox step as login<br/>is what proves the address is yours.<br/>The payment page offers a guest this route:<br/>the cart, and the order just placed, come along.
